## Seeded environment

Session start mirrors host essentials directly into the script
environment map; hardcoded fallbacks apply only when the host
lacks a value, and identity rows stay absent instead of invented.
Explicit script `ENV`/`INHERIT_ENV` overwrite entries uniformly;
`ISOLATED` resets the map to the same seed. Nothing injects at
spawn time and nothing is immutable: every default below is
overridable like any other variable.

### Host-mirrored defaults

Mirrored from the host at session start and on every `ISOLATED` entry; fallbacks apply only when the host lacks a value. Explicit script values win.

| Variable | Default source | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `PATH` | host value, else the platform baseline (`/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin`, `C:\Windows\System32;C:\Windows`) | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `TMPDIR` | host value, else session `<scratch>/tmp` | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `HOME` | host `HOME`, else host `USERPROFILE`, else session `<scratch>/tmp` | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `LOGNAME` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `USER` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `TERM` | host value, else `dumb` | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `TEMP` | host value, else session `<scratch>/tmp` | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `TMP` | host value, else session `<scratch>/tmp` | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `USERPROFILE` | host value, else session `<scratch>/tmp` (native profile anchor) | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `USERPROFILE` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `LOCALAPPDATA` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `APPDATA` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `SystemRoot` | host value, else the `C:\Windows` fallback | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `windir` | same root as `SystemRoot` | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `PATHEXT` | host value, else `.COM;.EXE;.BAT;.CMD` | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `ProgramFiles` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `ProgramFiles(x86)` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `ProgramW6432` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `COMSPEC` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `SystemDrive` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE` | host value; omitted when unset | seeded default: explicit script values win |
| `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` | session `<scratch>/target`, owned by cargo alone | seeded default: explicit script values win |

### Explicit routing

Essential variables (`PATH`, `HOME`/`USERPROFILE`, temp bindings,
loader anchors) mirror the host by default, with hardcoded
fallbacks only when the host lacks them. Everything else enters
scripts only when listed in `INHERIT_ENV` (inside `ISOLATED`, only
when listed in the block allowlist, which copies from the enclosing
scope). Absent stays absent.

### Host reads

Variables the engine process itself touches (not seeds into scripts).

| Variable | Read by | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SHELL` | oxdock_process::shell::shell_program | interactive shell resolution (`oxdock --shell`); batch steps pin `sh` |
| `COMSPEC` | oxdock_process::shell::shell_program | interactive shell resolution on Windows; batch steps pin `cmd` |
| `PATH` | seed_defaults | mirrored default; platform baseline when the host sets nothing |
| `HOME` | seed_defaults | mirrored default; session scratch when the host sets nothing |
| `USERPROFILE` | seed_defaults | mirrored default; session scratch when the host sets nothing |
| `TERM` | seed_defaults | seeded default; synthetic `dumb` when the host sets nothing |
| `SystemRoot` | seed_defaults | seeded default; fallback is the `C:\Windows` constant |
| `PATHEXT` | seed_defaults | seeded default; synthetic list when the host sets nothing |
| `HOME` | seed_transport | transport profile bridge only: the host value reaches `ssh` key discovery, never scripts |
| `USERPROFILE` | seed_transport | transport profile bridge only: the host value reaches `ssh.exe` key discovery, never scripts |
| `TMPDIR` | LazyGuardedTempDir::new (via std::env::temp_dir) | scratch root placement only; the value is never seeded |
| `CARGO_FEATURE_*` | BuiltinEnv::collect | sanctioned ambient seed: Cargo-namespaced feature flags |
| `CARGO_CFG_*` | BuiltinEnv::collect | sanctioned ambient seed: Cargo-namespaced cfg flags |

### Precedence and enforcement

Uniform script-wins: the seed populates defaults, and explicit
script `ENV`/`INHERIT_ENV` overwrite them like any other variable.
No name is immutable. `ISOLATED` resets to the identical seed, so
inner and outer scopes start from the same defaults.
`check_spawn_anchors` validates the final staged map with no
caller-specific flags: present anchors pass, absent ones bail
naming the `INHERIT_ENV` fix.

Source of truth: `crates/sys/oxdock-fs/src/env.rs` (names) and
`crates/sys/oxdock-process/src/env_policy.rs` (seeding). This
file is generated; do not edit by hand.

